Vulnerability class: Typo in constructor name — uninitialized owner.

Root cause: Solidity 0.6.x used function-name-based constructors. A single character typo made the constructor a public function callable by anyone.

Real world impact: Rubixi protocol, 2016. Developers renamed contract from DynamicPyramid to Rubixi but forgot to rename the constructor function. Attacker called it and drained funds.

Fix: Solidity 0.7.0+ introduced the constructor keyword specifically to prevent this. Never use function-name-based constructors.

solidity
// Vulnerable (0.6.x)
function Fallout() public payable {
    owner = msg.sender;
}

// Safe (0.7.0+)
constructor() public payable {
    owner = msg.sender;
}
